const tests = [
  '.history-detail .history-step-header + .conv-record::before',
  '.history-detail .conv-record:has(+ .history-step-header)::before',
  '.history-detail > .conv-record:first-child::before',
  '.history-detail > .conv-record:last-child::before',
];
for (const t of tests) {
  const idx = CSS.indexOf(t);
  console.log(idx === -1 ? 'MISSING: ' + t : 'FOUND at ' + idx + ': ' + t);
}
"

content.text:
My review is complete. Here are my findings:

```json
{
    "issues": [],
    "previous_issue_resolutions": [
        {
            "prev_issue_summary": "Boundary overflow-suppression rules have lower specificity (0,3,1) than the base ::before rule (0,5,1), so top:-7px/bottom:-7px always wins the cascade and the lane colour bleeds across step headers",
            "status": "fixed"
        }
    ],
    "summary": "The implementation is solid. The previously reported critical specificity issue has been correctly fixed by repeating `.history-detail` three times in each boundary rule selector, raising their specificity to (0,5,1) to match the base ::before rule. Since the boundary rules come later in source order, they win the cascade tiebreaker and correctly suppress the ±7px overflow at step headers and container edges. All 13 per-type rules preserve their original colour/alpha values (now on --step-lane instead of background), the ::before underlay bridges the 14px gap correctly (7px from each side meets at the midline), status markers remain excluded, and the change applies uniformly to both the running-flow and history-detail views (both carry .history-detail). The test file covers all four verification dimensions (a-d) and the existing mobile-responsive tests were correctly updated to check --step-lane instead of background:. No new issues found."
}
```

